{"at_ms": 6494, "body": {"answer": "Because most brokers resume from the last committed offset and redeliver in order, so after a reconnect the client replays the whole backlog (including any prefetched batch it had already pulled into memory) before the unacked message cycles back around \u2014 nothing jumps the queue. Redelivery also usually waits on a visibility/ack timeout to expire, and since that timer only starts once the message is actually re-exposed, the drain of everything ahead of it finishes first.", "model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "session_id": "dsflash:main"}, "dir": "in", "method": "session/btw", "wall_ms": 1790978454409}
